WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.820
Two crossovers can leave the outer markers looking untouched.

2
00:00:05.300 --> 00:00:07.980
How can offspring reveal a chromosome that switched twice?

3
00:00:11.533 --> 00:00:14.893
Follow one blue chromosome and one gold chromosome.

4
00:00:16.113 --> 00:00:18.713
Each carries three marker blocks in the same order.

5
00:00:19.933 --> 00:00:22.793
A red crossover point swaps the chromosome tails.

6
00:00:24.133 --> 00:00:27.193
One crossover changes the outer-marker combination.

7
00:00:28.573 --> 00:00:30.153
A second swap can restore it.

8
00:00:31.083 --> 00:00:34.203
Now place a green marker between the outer markers.

9
00:00:35.483 --> 00:00:39.543
After two swaps, the outer colours again match a parental chromosome.

10
00:00:40.903 --> 00:00:42.603
The green middle marker does not.

11
00:00:43.823 --> 00:00:45.743
It records the hidden double crossover.

12
00:00:46.917 --> 00:00:50.697
Cover the middle marker, and the double-switch product looks parental.

13
00:00:51.997 --> 00:00:53.797
Uncover it, and the mismatch appears.

14
00:00:55.137 --> 00:00:57.337
The chromosome did not change between views.

15
00:00:58.697 --> 00:01:01.937
The third observation changed what the cross could detect.

16
00:01:03.000 --> 00:01:07.040
A test cross turns these chromosome patterns into offspring classes.

17
00:01:08.400 --> 00:01:12.160
The recessive tester contributes the same alleles every time.

18
00:01:13.840 --> 00:01:18.340
Therefore each offspring phenotype reports one gamete from the heterozygous parent.

19
00:01:19.400 --> 00:01:21.760
Eight possible gametes become eight bars.

20
00:01:23.060 --> 00:01:27.240
The largest pair is provisionally parental, with no detected crossover.

21
00:01:28.500 --> 00:01:31.360
Two middle pairs represent single crossovers.

22
00:01:32.560 --> 00:01:35.720
The smallest pair is provisionally double crossovers.

23
00:01:36.700 --> 00:01:38.540
Rarity is a clue, not proof.

24
00:01:39.600 --> 00:01:44.160
Here are two parental patterns and two rare patterns from a schematic cross.

25
00:01:45.540 --> 00:01:47.020
Which marker must be in the middle?

26
00:01:48.540 --> 00:01:51.680
Compare each rare pattern with the parental it resembles most.

27
00:01:57.717 --> 00:02:00.497
Only marker C differs in each matched pair.

28
00:02:01.757 --> 00:02:04.897
So C belongs in the middle, even though it is written last.

29
00:02:06.157 --> 00:02:09.337
The changed marker decided the order, not the written order.

30
00:02:10.697 --> 00:02:14.697
Unequal survival could still make another class unusually small.

31
00:02:15.767 --> 00:02:20.787
Move the changed marker into the centre, then rewrite every class in map order.

32
00:02:22.147 --> 00:02:26.047
Each single-crossover pattern now changes colour in one interval.

33
00:02:27.387 --> 00:02:29.447
Each double changes in both intervals.

34
00:02:30.707 --> 00:02:32.387
The class list has become a map.

35
00:02:33.417 --> 00:02:36.317
Count each single crossover in its own interval.

36
00:02:37.657 --> 00:02:42.217
Count every double crossover in both intervals, because each double crossed both.

37
00:02:43.537 --> 00:02:48.497
Divide each interval count by the total offspring, and express it in centimorgans.

38
00:02:49.677 --> 00:02:52.717
The two adjacent distances then add along the map.

39
00:02:53.750 --> 00:02:55.450
Hide the green marker again.

40
00:02:56.790 --> 00:03:01.790
Both swaps restore the outer parental combination, so those doubles vanish from a

41
00:03:01.790 --> 00:03:05.270
two-point count. The map becomes too short.

42
00:03:06.470 --> 00:03:09.590
The middle marker is the witness that prevents that loss.

43
00:03:10.733 --> 00:03:15.133
This works when the classes are scorable and adjacent intervals are short.

44
00:03:16.573 --> 00:03:17.933
Long intervals can hide more.

45
00:03:19.493 --> 00:03:20.793
Rarity is a clue, not proof.

46
00:03:22.253 --> 00:03:25.833
Check that rare classes survive and form a reciprocal pair.

47
00:03:27.133 --> 00:03:29.853
A middle marker makes double crossovers visible.
